{"availability":"available","full":"hale-lang/hale","name":"hale","description":"A general-purpose, native, memory-safe language for scripts, services, and systems. As a program grows, ownership, concurrency, placement, and effects become things the compiler checks, not conventions.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Rust","stars":39,"forks":2,"created":"2026-05-15T02:57:23Z","updated":"2026-10-09T05:35:21Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://hale-lang.org","topics":["agents","compiler","concurrency","effect-system","formal-verification","llvm","low-latency","message-passing","model-checking","no-gc","programming-language","static-analysis","systems-programming","wasm"],"demo":"https://hale-lang.org/playground","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T05:46:41.535Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T05:46:41.535Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T05:46:41.535Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T22:13:41.270Z","stars":38,"forks":2},{"at":"2026-10-04T21:35:05.254Z","stars":38,"forks":2},{"at":"2026-10-06T22:53:46.975Z","stars":38,"forks":2},{"at":"2026-10-09T05:46:41.535Z","stars":39,"forks":2}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["One language from a five-line script to a dynamic distributed system.","hale-lang.org · Guide · Playground · Packages · Features · Glossary","Hale is a compiled, general-purpose language. Every piece of state has one owner, and the parts of a program talk only over declared, typed message channels. That shape lets the compiler check a program's architecture the way it checks its types. It runs natively with no garbage collector and no borrow checker, and its concurrency has no locks and no data races."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/hale-lang/hale/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"e8f94b4f0a805f9eaf119209a75e03be945f82bcc1b37b494f44986925c1e175","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T23:12:44.984Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T23:12:44.984Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"One language from a five-line script to a dynamic distributed system.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/hale-lang/hale/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"paid_service","status":"required","text":"Architecture is a property of the whole graph: \"billing must never reach research\", \"exactly one thing writes settlements\", and saying that with per-function contracts means scattering them across every position and hoping you got them all.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/hale-lang/hale/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"paid_service","status":"optional","text":"Six forms cover the shapes worth stating. forbid reaches(A, B) for absence, optionally narrowed via { calls } or via { bus }; require subscribes(some G, topic T) for existence; count publishers(topic T) B { publish T; } for a reviewable boundary inventory; and bound llm <= N on paths from G for cost. bound counts a user-declared effect class (effect llm;): the counted…","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/hale-lang/hale/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"hosting","status":"documented","text":"The proven core, all of it self-hosted by the native compiler: the typed topic bus; placement, bindings and NUMA-aware topology with replicas; @form collections; structural interfaces; @ffi C bindings; the fallible(T) error model; effects and budgets; claims, constitutions and fleet composition; the canonical model (hale model, its diff and its verification); record and…","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/hale-lang/hale/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"e8f94b4f0a805f9eaf119209a75e03be945f82bcc1b37b494f44986925c1e175","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/hale-lang/hale/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T23:12:44.986Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-09T05:35:21Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/hale-lang/hale/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T23:12:44.989Z","hash":"e8f94b4f0a805f9eaf119209a75e03be945f82bc